I attempted two independent prior-art searches to verify collisions; both were permission-blocked, so I reason from the packet's cited sources (treated as evidence of record per committee rules) plus the well-established CWE/SWC taxonomy.

```
ROLE: novelty_killer  VOTE: yellow

CLOSEST_PRIOR_WORK:
- {cite: "CWE-330 Use of Insufficiently Random Values", url: "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/330.html", why_close: "The exact failure class — a non-cryptographic / predictable RNG standing in for a CSPRNG. wazero's fixed-seed math/rand backing random_get is a textbook CWE-330 instance; the bug class is owned."}
- {cite: "SWC-120 Weak Sources of Randomness from Chain Attributes", url: "https://swcregistry.io/docs/SWC-120", why_close: "Deterministic-environment-demotes-RNG is the EVM analogue the packet itself cites; the deterministic-host-forces-predictable-entropy pattern is prior, documented hazard, not new."}
- {cite: "CrowdSec PR#4495 + wetware issue#106 (practitioner find+fix of the exact wazero random_get composition)", url: "(packet-cited; web verify blocked)", why_close: "TWO INDEPENDENT practitioners hit and FIXED this precise wazero fixed-seed-random_get composition. This is the decisive collision: the specific mechanism, not just the class, is already discovered and remediated in the wild."}
- {cite: "wapc/wapc-go (mature host that explicitly fixed this composition)", url: "(packet-cited)", why_close: "A THIRD independent host already remediated the identical default. Confirms the mechanism is known-and-being-fixed."}
- {cite: "WASI preview1 random_get witx + wasi:random/random successor spec + Rust getrandom docs", url: "https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI", why_close: "The conformance contract the claim leans on is pre-existing published spec text; the claim reads it, it does not author it."}

NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: Mostly NAMING/re-framing, not a new mechanism. The underlying mechanism (deterministic default silently substitutes a predictable PRNG for the WASI entropy syscall + frozen clocks) is owned three times over by independent practitioner find-and-fix (CrowdSec, wetware, wapc-go) and classed by CWE-330/SWC-120. What is genuinely un-owned is the SYNTHESIS framing — "silent CSPRNG demotion at the ABI boundary, cross-language + cross-runtime-anomalous + un-defendable-by-correct-guest-code + clock-decoupling half, argued as a spec-conformance differential." That is a real analytical packaging of known facts, but it is characterization, not a new mechanism delta. Mechanism novelty is capped by the find-and-fix evidence.

FATAL_COLLISIONS: None that is singular/total — no prior paper or CVE performs the full synthesis (ABI + cross-lang + cross-runtime-anomaly + conformance argument + clock half) as one artifact, so this is NOT a RED kill. But the core hazard collides with ≥3 independent practitioner remediations (CrowdSec PR#4495, wetware issue#106, wapc/wapc-go), which is a verified-in-≥2-sources collision against MECHANISM novelty — enough to deny GREEN.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: [CWE-330; SWC-120; CrowdSec PR#4495; wetware issue#106; wapc/wapc-go remediation; WASI preview1 random_get witx ("high-quality" + blocking clause); wasi:random/random successor spec ("cryptographically secure", "deterministic environments must OMIT"); wasi:random/insecure; Rust getrandom backend docs; wazero config.go (WithRandSource / WithWalltime / Nanotime / Nanosleep defaults)]. The authors MUST position the contribution explicitly AGAINST the practitioner find-fix set and CWE-330/SWC-120 and frame the delta as conformance-synthesis, not discovery.

RATIONALE: My role is to kill weak novelty. The mechanism here is NOT new: three independent practitioner sources (CrowdSec PR#4495, wetware issue#106, wapc/wapc-go) discovered AND fixed the identical wazero fixed-seed random_get composition, and the bug class is CWE-330/SWC-120. That satisfies the ≥2-independent-source bar for a mechanism collision and forecloses GREEN on novelty grounds. However, no single prior artifact performs the claim's full SYNTHESIS — the cross-runtime conformance differential (wazero anomalous vs Wasmtime/Wasmer's CSPRNG defaults) + the un-defendable-by-correct-guest argument + the clock-decoupling half, argued from verbatim spec — so there is no fatal singular collision and RED is not warranted. Net: the spec-conformance + cross-runtime arms are real and clear the folklore gate, but the contribution is known-hazard re-characterization (NAMING-leaning) rather than a new mechanism, capping it at YELLOW pending the L2 (authenticated prevalence + blast-radius), which is what would convert characterization into a measured, citable systemic finding. Honest YELLOW is the zero-false-green outcome here.
